\tan \left(\frac{\theta}{2}\right) = \left|\frac{1 - \cos \theta}{\sin \theta}\right| \sqrt{1 + \frac{1 - \cos \theta}{\sin \theta}} = \left|\frac{1 - \cos \theta}{\sin \theta}\right| \sqrt{\frac{2}{1 + \cos \theta}}.
]\]We know that $\cos 15^\circ = \frac{\sqrt{6} + \sqrt{2}}{4}$ and $\sin 15^\circ = \frac{\sqrt{6} - \sqrt{2}}{4}$, so we can plug these values into the formula to get \[
\tan 7.5^\circ = \left|\frac{1 - \cos 15^\circ}{\sin 15^\circ}\right| \sqrt{\frac{2}{1 + \cos 15^\circ}} = \boxed{4}.
]\]

